NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000001 "package Carton;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000002 "use strict;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000003 "use 5.008_005;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000004 "use version; our $VERSION = version->declare(\"v1.0.35\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000005 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000006 "1;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000007 "__END__"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000008 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000009 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000010 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000011 "Carton - Perl module dependency manager (aka Bundler for Perl)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000012 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000013 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000014 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000015 "  # On your development environment"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000016 "  > cat cpanfile"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000017 "  requires 'Plack', '0.9980';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000018 "  requires 'Starman', '0.2000';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000019 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000020 "  > carton install"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000021 "  > git add cpanfile cpanfile.snapshot"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000022 "  > git commit -m \"add Plack and Starman\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000023 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000024 "  # Other developer's machine, or on a deployment box"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000025 "  > carton install"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000026 "  > carton exec starman -p 8080 myapp.psgi"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000027 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000028 "  # carton exec is optional"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000029 "  > perl -Ilocal/lib/perl5 local/bin/starman -p 8080 myapp.psgi"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000030 "  > PERL5LIB=/path/to/local/lib/perl5 /path/to/local/bin/starman -p 8080 myapp.psgi"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 "=head1 AVAILABILITY"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 "Carton only works with perl installation with the complete set of core"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 "modules. If you use perl installed by a vendor package with modules"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 "stripped from core, Carton is not expected to work correctly."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 "Also, Carton requires you to run your command/application with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 "C<carton exec> command or to include the I<local/lib/perl5> directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 "in your Perl library search path (using C<PERL5LIB>, C<-I>, or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 "L<lib>)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 "carton is a command line tool to track the Perl module dependencies"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 "for your Perl application. Dependencies are declared using L<cpanfile>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 "format, and the managed dependencies are tracked in a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 "I<cpanfile.snapshot> file, which is meant to be version controlled,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 "and the snapshot file allows other developers of your application will"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 "have the exact same versions of the modules."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 "For C<cpanfile> syntax, see L<cpanfile> documentation."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000054 "=head1 TUTORIAL"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000055 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000056 "=head2 Initializing the environment"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000057 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000058 "carton will use the I<local> directory to install modules into. You're"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000059 "recommended to exclude these directories from the version control"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000060 "system."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000061 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000062 "  > echo local/ >> .gitignore"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000063 "  > git add cpanfile cpanfile.snapshot"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000064 "  > git commit -m \"Start using carton\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000065 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000066 "=head2 Tracking the dependencies"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000067 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000068 "You can manage the dependencies of your application via C<cpanfile>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000069 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000070 "  # cpanfile"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000071 "  requires 'Plack', '0.9980';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000072 "  requires 'Starman', '0.2000';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000073 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000074 "And then you can install these dependencies via:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000075 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000076 "  > carton install"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000077 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000078 "The modules are installed into your I<local> directory, and the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000079 "dependencies tree and version information are analyzed and saved into"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000080 "I<cpanfile.snapshot> in your directory."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000081 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000082 "Make sure you add I<cpanfile> and I<cpanfile.snapshot> to your version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000083 "controlled repository and commit changes as you update"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000084 "dependencies. This will ensure that other developers on your app, as"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000085 "well as your deployment environment, use exactly the same versions of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000086 "the modules you just installed."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000087 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000088 "  > git add cpanfile cpanfile.snapshot"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000089 "  > git commit -m \"Added Plack and Starman\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000090 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000091 "=head2 Specifying a CPAN distribution"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000092 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000093 "You can pin a module resolution to a specific distribution using a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000094 "combination of C<dist>, C<mirror> and C<url> options in C<cpanfile>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000095 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000096 "  # specific distribution on PAUSE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000097 "  requires 'Plack', '== 0.9980',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000098 "    dist => 'MIYAGAWA/Plack-0.9980.tar.gz';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000099 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000100 "  # local mirror (darkpan)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000101 "  requires 'Plack', '== 0.9981',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000102 "    dist => 'MYCOMPANY/Plack-0.9981-p1.tar.gz',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000103 "    mirror => 'https://pause.local/';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000104 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000105 "  # URL"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000106 "  requires 'Plack', '== 1.1000',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000107 "    url => 'https://pause.local/authors/id/M/MY/MYCOMPANY/Plack-1.1000.tar.gz';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000108 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000109 "=head2 Deploying your application"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000110 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000111 "Once you've done installing all the dependencies, you can push your"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000112 "application directory to a remote machine (excluding I<local> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000113 "I<.carton>) and run the following command:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000114 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000115 "  > carton install --deployment"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000116 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000117 "This will look at the I<cpanfile.snapshot> and install the exact same"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000118 "versions of the dependencies into I<local>, and now your application"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000119 "is ready to run."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000120 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000121 "The C<--deployment> flag makes sure that carton will only install"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000122 "modules and versions available in your snapshot, and won't fallback to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000123 "query for CPAN Meta DB for missing modules."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000124 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000125 "=head2 Bundling modules"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000126 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000127 "carton can bundle all the tarballs for your dependencies into a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000128 "directory so that you can even install dependencies that are not"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000129 "available on CPAN, such as internal distribution aka DarkPAN."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000130 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000131 "  > carton bundle"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000132 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000133 "will bundle these tarballs into I<vendor/cache> directory, and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000134 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000135 "  > carton install --cached"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000136 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000137 "will install modules using this local cache. Combined with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000138 "C<--deployment> option, you can avoid querying for a database like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000139 "CPAN Meta DB or downloading files from CPAN mirrors upon deployment"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000140 "time."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000141 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000142 "As of Carton v1.0.32, the bundle also includes a package index"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000143 "allowing you to simply use L<cpanm> (which has a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000144 "L<standalone version|App::cpanminus/\"Downloading the standalone executable\">)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000145 "instead of installing Carton on a remote machine."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000146 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000147 "  > cpanm -L local --from \"$PWD/vendor/cache\" --installdeps --notest --quiet ."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000148 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000149 "=head1 PERL VERSIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000150 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000151 "When you take a snapshot in one perl version and deploy on another"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000152 "(different) version, you might have troubles with core modules."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000153 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000154 "The simplest solution, which might not work for everybody, is to use"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000155 "the same version of perl in the development and deployment."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000156 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000157 "To enforce that, you're recommended to use L<plenv> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000158 "C<.perl-version> to lock perl versions in development."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000159 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000160 "You can also specify the minimum perl required in C<cpanfile>:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000161 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000162 "  requires 'perl', '5.16.3';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000163 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000164 "and carton (and cpanm) will give you errors when deployed on hosts"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000165 "with perl lower than the specified version."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000166 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000167 "=head1 COMMUNITY"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000168 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000169 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000170 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000171 "=item L<https://github.com/perl-carton/carton>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000172 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000173 "Code repository, Wiki and Issue Tracker"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000174 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000175 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000176 ""
